f-window, while another member (1163) gains the same large neighbor set in the post window. This synchronous reassignment of an external contact set from some group members to others within the short boundary is consistent with an abrupt regime switch of partners rather than gradual turnover. Controls show that overall activity volume is not the sole cause (step_02), the group is active (step_01), and some static connections persist for some nodes (1036, steps_07-08), so the change is temporal reallocation of contacts among group members."}, "raw_final_response": "{\n  \"task_id\": \"t_25544f86\",\n  \"decision\": \"present\",\n  \"mechanism\": \"regime_switch\",\n  \"entities\": [25, 396, 489, 638, 1036, 1163, 1244, 1366, 1417, 1489, 1729, 1763],\n  \"window\": [9140, 39140],\n  \"confidence\": 0.8,\n  \"evidence\": [\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_19\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_20\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_21\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_22\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_23\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_24\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_03\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_04\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_05\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_06\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_09\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_10\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_07\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_08\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_01\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_02\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"}\n  ],\n  \"narrative\": \"Comparing the two half-windows around the candidate change point (~19140): several group members (e.g. 489, 638, 25, 396, 1763) have many neighbors in the pre-change half-window and zero in the post-change half-window, while another member (1163) gains the same large neighbor set in the post window. This synchronous reassignment of an external contact set from some group members to others within the short boundary is consistent with an abrupt regime switch of partners rather than gradual turnover. Controls show that overall activity volume is not the sole cause (step_02), the group is active (step_01), and some static connections persist for some nodes (1036, steps_07-08), so the change is temporal reallocation of contacts among group members.\"\n}", "total_input_tokens": 13241, "total_output_tokens": 8497, "total_tokens": 21738, "total_latency_ms": 90957, "llm_calls": 5, "schema_repairs": 0, "status": "success", "error": ""}